---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { SITE, url, HAS_EMAIL } from '../site';
import { TOOLS } from '../data/tools';

const guides = await getCollection('guides', (g) => !g.data.draft);
const en = guides.filter((g) => g.data.lang === 'en').length;
const ur = guides.filter((g) => g.data.lang === 'ur').length;
---
<Prose title="About us" description={`What ${SITE.name} is and how it works: practical, checked guides for expats in Saudi Arabia, in English and Urdu.`} path="about/">
  <p>{SITE.name} explains Saudi procedures step by step for expats: iqama, visas, Absher, labor law, driving and daily life. Every guide links the official source it relies on and shows the date it was last checked. The most-used guides are also available in Urdu.</p>

  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>Most official information about Saudi procedures is in Arabic or spread across several government portals, and much of what gets forwarded in WhatsApp groups is out of date. {SITE.name} puts each procedure in one place: what you need, the steps in order, the fees, and the mistakes that cost people time and money. It is written in Saudi Arabia for people who live and work here.</p>

  <h2>What you will find</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>{en} step-by-step guides in English, and {ur} in Urdu, with more Urdu guides added every week.</li>
    <li>{TOOLS.length} free calculators, including iqama fees, end-of-service benefit, exit re-entry visa fees, overtime and annual leave.</li>
    <li>Short news updates when a fee, rule or deadline changes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We start every guide from the official portal or ministry: Absher, Qiwa, MOFA, MHRSD, Jawazat and others.</li>
    <li>Each guide shows a "last checked" date. We recheck the most-read guides regularly and whenever a rule changes.</li>
    <li>We fix confirmed errors and note the correction on the page. See our <a href={url('editorial-policy/')}>editorial policy</a> and <a href={url('corrections/')}>corrections policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we are not</h2>
  <p>{SITE.name} is an independent website. It is not affiliated with the Saudi government, any ministry, or any embassy. Our guides explain procedures; they are not legal advice. Always confirm on the official portal before you act.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  {HAS_EMAIL
    ? <p>Questions, corrections or suggestions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
    : <p>Questions, corrections or suggestions: see our <a href={url('contact/')}>contact page</a>.</p>}
</Prose>
